    {
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 15, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 31 },
      "id": 22,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## The four token types — and why price changes everything\n\nEvery number here is built from four token types. They do the same job but cost\nwildly different amounts, so **token share and cost share never match**.\n\n| type | what it is | price vs `input` | Opus 4.8 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cacheRead` | context replayed from cache | **0.1x** | $0.50 /MTok |\n| `input` | fresh tokens the cache didn't cover | 1x | $5 /MTok |\n| `cacheCreation` | context written into the cache | **1.25x** | $6.25 /MTok |\n| `output` | tokens generated — **thinking counts here** | **5x** | $25 /MTok |\n\nOne `output` token costs **50x** one `cacheRead` token. That's why the two pies\nabove look nothing alike, and why the cost pie is the one to read.\n\n## Targets\n\n| number | aim for | bad sign |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Cache amortization** | **> 5x**, ideally 10x+ | **< 1x** — paying for cache you never reuse |\n| **Cache write % of cost** | < 30% | > 50% — sessions dying before they amortize |\n| **Generation intensity** | 1–3% | > 5% — heavy generation or high-effort thinking |\n| **Uncached input** | < 1% | > 5% — something is defeating the prefix cache |\n\n**Don't drive `cacheCreation` to zero.** Writes are the cost of admission: no\nwrites means no cheap reads and a *bigger* bill. Caching breaks even after ~1.3\nreuses, so the goal is a high read/write ratio — not a low write count.\n\n## If a number goes the wrong way\n\n**Cache write % climbing** — ranked by impact:\n1. **Too many short sessions.** Each fresh session rebuilds the cache. Use\n   `claude --continue` instead of starting over. *Biggest lever.*\n2. **Long idle gaps.** The cache expires; the next turn re-writes the prefix.\n3. **Context churn.** Cache is a *prefix* match — changing something early\n   invalidates everything after it.\n4. **Model switching mid-task.** Caches are per-model.\n\n**Generation intensity climbing** — lower effort where the task doesn't need it;\nmake targeted edits instead of whole-file rewrites; stop asking for recaps you\nwon't read.\n\n**Cost per session climbing** — check it against session count. Fewer, longer\nsessions *should* raise it. Only worry if total cost rises too.\n\n## What this dashboard can't tell you\n\n**Your plan usage / rate limits are not here and can't be.** Claude Code exports\nno quota, limit, or plan-tier data — not as a metric, not as an event, and it\nisn't persisted in transcripts or any local file. `/usage` queries Anthropic\nlive and never stores the result, so there's nothing to scrape.\n\nUse **`/usage` in Claude Code** for \"how much runway is left\" — it's live and\nauthoritative. Use **this dashboard** for \"what is burning it\". Improving the\nfour ratios above is what makes the runway last longer.\n\nPrices are **API-equivalent** — on a subscription this is not your bill, it's a\nconsistent yardstick for comparing sessions and habits. Full detail:\n`docs/METRICS-GUIDE.md`.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.4.0",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "transparent": false,
      "type": "text"
    },
